  "name": "QSOL-SUBSTRATE",
  "description": "A public, vendor-neutral, deterministic and provenance-aware context substrate for AI systems. QSOL-SUBSTRATE separates canonical public facts from derived adapters, tool-less capsules, vector retrieval, latent/prefix experiment contracts, evaluation reports, release manifests, and archival metadata. Its core open-world semantic rule is that absence from the public substrate means unavailable, not false.",
